{"name":"Velvet Curtain","hex":"#7e85a3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"velvet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with velvet or with a covering of a similar texture.","To coat raw meat in starch, then in oil, preparatory to frying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet"},{"term":"curtain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of cloth covering a window, bed, etc. to offer privacy and keep out light.","A similar piece of cloth that separates the audience and the stage in a theater."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover (a window) with a curtain; to hang curtains.","To hide, cover or separate as if by a curtain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curtain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet"},{"title":"Curtain","blocks":[{"text":"A curtain is a piece of cloth or other material intended to block or obscure light, air drafts, or water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Gordijnen_aan_venster.JPG/330px-Gordijnen_aan_venster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curtain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org